china's 2022 party congress is expected  to be a landmark with all eyes on the  country's leader xi jinping here's why  xi jinping is expected to disrupt the  way that power transitions in china this  year exceeding the normal two-time limit  to take a third time in power despite  the fact he exceeded the country's  normal retirement age of 68 in june  when xi jinping came into power he  stated that he wanted to achieve the  great rejuvenation of the chinese nation  which was to make it a world power again  on the global stage so far in terms of  the economy china's on track now to  surpass the us  as the world's largest in the next 10  years china has the world's largest navy  and xi jinping's flagship belt and road  foreign policy initiative has built  influence and infrastructure all around  the world however under xi china has  become more closed the internet has  become far more regulated and he's  overseen a campaign of oppression in  xinjiang which the us has called  genocide a crackdown on freedoms in hong  kong and put pressure on taiwan all of  that has fractured relations with the  west and more recently his covert zero  policy after being so successful at  containing deaths in the early pandemic  is giving china's economy a real  bruising  some 2 000 delegates from all across  china will descend on beijing these  include top military officials  provincial party leaders farming  representatives and people from china's  minority groups they'll huddle behind  closed doors for five days and decide  everything from policy priorities to  sort of who's leading the country  although actually much of that has been  decided beforehand but only at the end  of the congress afterwards xi jinping  will walk out in a sort of press  conference with his top cabinet behind  him in order of rank and only then will  people really understand who it is that  xi jinping and the party have selected  to be the country's most powerful men  [Music]  xi jinping has overseen an  anti-corruption campaign in the past 10  years which has pretty much eliminated  all of his rivals however there are  still a few rising stars and it will be  interesting to see what position they  land in these include chen minou and  huchenhua who are long time shi  associates  people will also be very closely  watching where li tiang ends up this is  the shanghai party secretary he is a  close sheet ally he was tipped to enter  the politburo standing committee but  after overseeing a pretty disastrous  kobe campaign in shanghai there are  rumors that he might no longer get a  promotion
 

